{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994384989491001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"irongray-profound-abalone","assignee":"","attestations":{"completion-verifier":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"e33a31577351c3a0f3965c311f0e14df48d60e41","key_id":null,"kind":"completion-verifier","manifest":["completion-verifier: PASS","ticket: c130-6a87-531e-4441","model: anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","rebar-version: 0.7.1 (e33a31577)","material: 4d839103b1ce067a","verified-at-sha:e33a31577351c3a0f3965c311f0e14df48d60e41"],"material_fingerprint":"4d839103b1ce067a","merged_log_commit":"e33a31577351c3a0f3965c311f0e14df48d60e41","principal":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","signature":null,"signed_at":1784161327101014000},"plan-review":{"algorithm":"sshsig","author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","envelope":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.opcert.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","head_sha":"72bb4965e3781259f2b9791c8d3c67c23c79e93d","key_id":null,"kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: c130-6a87-531e-4441","material: 4d839103b1ce067a","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 12","rebar-version: 0.7.1 (72bb4965e)","regver: b293b9a55de591cc","verified-at-sha:72bb4965e3781259f2b9791c8d3c67c23c79e93d","dep 0b1ea57e9855741b87a1d5a54332f710fc2e4007c6b5847e665c2f3ad9c59e11 src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","dep 0d194db48ceeffcadaf27b165815b3973dc0345c5b0686e96cbcfa44d540d42f tests/unit/test_review_bot.py"],"material_fingerprint":"4d839103b1ce067a","merged_log_commit":"72bb4965e3781259f2b9791c8d3c67c23c79e93d","principal":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","signature":null,"signed_at":1784158504271370000}},"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":7},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"dc2f0e4b7f4ae9176ea8bf56238d6fc062822e65f7b24ea93dea8eeaf599b1b6","event_uuid":"8aa20943-e826-420e-8562-a757831b707e","position":{"commit_sha":"fda845728257ad68ef9e4390410f520fda245d79","position":"1784231775191393094-8aa20943-e826-420e-8562-a757831b707e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-210_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"04a4ea6e-bf84-4b9f-a45f-fb3e3d1d1d89","comments":[],"created_at":1784158135764175001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"The review-bot's structured operational logs (the `_emit()` INFO events —\n`voter_voted`, `voter_skip`, `merge_detection`, and all `reconcile_*`) are silently\ndropped in production, so operators are blind to what the bot decides. Configure a\nlogging handler for rebar's loggers so these reach stdout/journald.\n\n## Why\n`src/rebar/review_bot/` contains NO logging setup (`grep` for `basicConfig`/`dictConfig`\nin `src/rebar/` returns nothing). The container runs `uvicorn rebar.review_bot.app:app`;\nuvicorn configures only its own `uvicorn.*` loggers and never the root or `rebar.*`\nloggers. So a `logging.getLogger(\"rebar.review_bot.voter\").info(...)` record has no\nhandler and falls through to Python's `logging.lastResort`, which emits **WARNING and\nabove only** — every INFO `_emit` line is discarded. This was directly observed during\nincident triage: `journalctl` showed uvicorn's own access lines and the `print()`-to-stderr\nmarkers (`VOTER_ERROR`, `ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR`) but ZERO `voter_voted`/`reconcile_*` lines,\nmaking a healthy-but-slow reconciler look dead. The `_emit` docstrings call these\n\"observability markers\" — dropping them violates that documented intent.\n\n## What\nAdd a `_configure_logging()` to `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py`, called once at module import\n(before `app = FastAPI(...)`), that attaches a `StreamHandler(sys.stdout)` to the `rebar`\nlogger at level `INFO` (overridable via a `REVIEW_BOT_LOG_LEVEL` env var), with a bare\n`\"%(message)s\"` formatter (the `_emit` payload is already JSON), an idempotency marker on the\nhandler (so repeated imports/reloads don't stack handlers), and `propagate=False` (so records\ndo NOT double-log through uvicorn/root). Targeting the `rebar` logger specifically — not root\n— avoids duplicating uvicorn's access logs.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/review_bot/app.py`: add `_configure_logging()` + `import sys`; call at import.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`: add a test asserting a `rebar.review_bot.*` INFO record\n  reaches stdout after the app module configures logging (RED before the fix).\n- Non-goal (separate follow-up): shipping logs to a shared service (CloudWatch Logs group).\n  This change makes the logs *emitted*; centralizing them is tracked separately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A `logging.getLogger(\"rebar.review_bot.voter\").info(...)` record is written to stdout\n      once the review-bot app module has configured logging; before the fix the same record\n      produces no stdout output (proving the drop).\n      Proving command: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -k configure_logging -q`\n      passes, and the test is confirmed RED on the pre-fix tree.\n- [ ] The handler is idempotent: importing/configuring twice does not attach a second handler\n      (no duplicate log lines).\n      Proving command: assert `len([h for h in logging.getLogger(\"rebar\").handlers if marker])\n      == 1` after two `_configure_logging()` calls (in the test).\n- [ ] `REVIEW_BOT_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG` lowers the effective level (env override honored); an\n      absent/invalid value falls back to INFO.\n      Proving command: covered by a parametrized assertion in the test.\n- [ ] Existing gates stay green.\n      Proving command: `make lint && make typecheck && python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py -q` all exit 0.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/app.py","reason":"add _configure_logging() called at import"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot.py","reason":"RED test for rebar INFO reaching stdout"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"91d4e133-14d9-4ec2-8dc1-7d3f747db137","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c130-6a87-531e-4441","ticket_type":"task","title":"review-bot: configure logging so structured _emit INFO events reach stdout/journald","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b7b1ef98-f08b-43c1-b460-5d4fed215618","37eb001a-aaa0-4994-b009-456a050e3327","87d32739-383e-41c0-8f2f-10199a533536","8517dabc-105c-4dd9-a84d-813b2d9ae9b9","669c18e9-232e-48a2-83a2-a3ebcf9bea18","f6510cc7-4d53-470b-9e42-9c8df8250312","0366f608-dc17-46fd-84b4-dc60abdfe24d","91d4e133-14d9-4ec2-8dc1-7d3f747db137","29b5b440-48bb-4afe-bf83-51e68e7cbcaf","f74dcec1-3cdb-4959-aeda-5f2a80f9ce67","46c3ab9d-017e-430a-98e1-20c00d7db6cb","8aa20943-e826-420e-8562-a757831b707e","3935ad12-05bb-48c6-8ba2-4c03ac0e9b21","c3c8cc36-585a-480e-9c73-8f9246e9e709","9fdaed42-13a6-43d6-8e36-a56b28294ef1","f0dc31ee-a182-4fc4-8b3a-62c200753ee2"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994384989491001,"uuid":"2e3c728d-6a5a-400d-b3eb-95b27c4d3767"}